The Z-Machine Standards Document, version 1.1 (24 February 2014)
----------------------------------------------------------------
Graham Nelson, with revisions by Kevin Bracey, Jason C. Penney and
David Fillmore.

  https://www.inform-fiction.org/zmachine/standards/current/

The text is reproduced with corrections limited to clause numbering; every
such correction is listed in the revision note at the foot of the preface,
and in the "Defects found in the source" table in README.md. The pristine
2014 files this edition is generated from are kept in source/.

The section icons in images/ (icon01..icon16 and friends) and the memory-map
diagram are from the same document.

The Z and Q title letters that head the Standard and Quetzal were originally
low-resolution GIFs. They have been redrawn for this edition as images/zlogo.svg
and images/qlogo.svg, sharing one set of metrics with the B drawn for Blorb.
Those three SVGs are original work. The GIFs they replace are kept, unused, in
source/images/.


Quetzal: a common format for saved games, version 1.4 (13 November 1997)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Martin Frost. HTML typesetting by Graham Nelson.

  https://inform-fiction.org/zmachine/standards/quetzal/index.html

Reproduced verbatim as quetzal.html. Also includes images/qlogo.gif.


Blorb: an IF resource collection format, version 2.0.4
-------------------------------------------------------
Andrew Plotkin.

  https://www.eblong.com/zarf/blorb/blorb.html

Reproduced verbatim as blorb.html.

Blorb has never had a logo. The "B" shown at the top of that page
(images/blogo.svg) was drawn for this edition so that Blorb has a title mark
alongside the Z and Q of the other two documents. It is original work, not
Andrew Plotkin's, and is not official Blorb branding.


The Bocfel Adaptive Palette Chunk (the 'BPal' extension to Blorb)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Chris Spiegel, documented alongside snavig, the tool that writes it.

  https://github.com/cspiegel/snavig/blob/master/Blorb.md

Reproduced verbatim as the addendum at blorb.html#bpal, under the MIT licence
snavig carries. It is an unofficial extension: Andrew Plotkin has not adopted
it, and it is not part of Blorb. It is set apart on the page and marked as
such. The Markdown original is kept in source/bpal-original.md.


